{"name":"Buff Tone","hex":"#e8d0b9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Undyed leather from the skin of buffalo or similar animals.","A tool, often one covered with buff leather, used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the color of buff leather, a brownish yellow.","Unusually muscular."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buff"},{"term":"tone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A specific pitch.","(in the diatonic scale) An interval of a major second."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to give a particular tone to","to change the colour of"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buff (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a light brownish yellow, ochreous colour, typical of buff leather. Buff is a mixture of yellow ochre and white: two parts of white lead and one part of yellow ochre produces a good buff, or white lead may be tinted with French ochre alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Chamois-natural.jpg/330px-Chamois-natural.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2085487"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https